<title>CHINA: China imports 67,000 tonnes of New Zealand wool.</title>
<headline>China imports 67,000 tonnes of New Zealand wool.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China is now the biggest single importer of New Zealand wool, importing 67,000 tonnes in 1995/96, or 37 percent of total its wool exports, the China Daily said on Friday.</p>
<p>China's wool industry consumes about 350,000 tonnes a year, but the country can only supply about 70,000-80,000 tonnes from domestic sources, forcing it to import about 80 percent of demand, the newspaper quoted the China National Textile Council as saying.</p>
<p>The report gave no more details.</p>
</text>
